// Package client option categorization guide
//
// This document categorizes Kitex client options by their application scope:
// - Unary RPC options
// - Streaming RPC options  
// - TTHeader-Streaming specific options
//
// Most options apply to both unary and streaming RPCs unless noted otherwise.

package client

// UNARY RPC OPTIONS
// These options are primarily designed for unary (request-response) RPC patterns:
//
// Core unary options:
//   - WithShortConnection: Disables connection pooling, creates new connection per request
//   - WithRPCTimeout: Sets overall RPC timeout for unary calls
//   - WithConnectTimeout: Connection establishment timeout
//   - WithRetryPolicy: Retry configuration for failed unary calls
//   - WithFailureRetry: Enables basic retry on failure
//   - WithBackupRequest: Hedged requests for latency-sensitive unary RPCs
//   - WithFallback: Fallback handler when unary RPC fails
//
// STREAMING RPC OPTIONS
// These options apply specifically to streaming RPCs:
//
// Streaming-specific options:
//   - WithGRPCConnectTimeout: gRPC connection timeout for streaming
//   - WithGRPCKeepaliveParams: gRPC keepalive configuration for long-lived streams
//   - WithGRPCInitialWindowSize: Flow control window size for streams
//   - WithGRPCInitialConnWindowSize: Connection-level flow control
//   - WithGRPCMaxHeaderListSize: Header size limit for streaming metadata
//   - WithGRPCWriteBufferSize: Stream write buffer configuration
//   - WithGRPCReadBufferSize: Stream read buffer configuration
